# Cloudflare Pages headers. The TON Connect spec requires the manifest (and icon)
# to be readable from any origin — wallets fetch them cross-origin.

# Security headers for every page. The app has no backend: this page builds every
# transaction and holds the delivery codes, so script injection and framing by
# other sites must be shut out here.
#   - connect-src / img-src stay open to any https host: TON Connect talks to
#     dozens of wallet bridges and shows each wallet's icon, and the list changes.
#   - frame-ancestors lets only the Telegram web client frame the app.
# 'wasm-unsafe-eval' lets the fee emulator (src/ton/emulateFee.js) compile its
# WebAssembly; without it confirm, claim and a Funding cancel fail to price. It
# allows no eval of JavaScript. Any violation shows on the hidden /debug screen.
# static.cloudflareinsights.com serves the Cloudflare Web Analytics beacon that
# Pages adds to every HTML page; it reports to cloudflareinsights.com, which
# connect-src https: already allows.
# script-src-attr lets through only EMPTY inline handlers (the hash is of the
# empty string): TON Connect UI sets ontouchstart="" on body so :active works on
# iOS Safari. Any handler with code in it is still blocked.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' https://telegram.org https://static.cloudflareinsights.com 'wasm-unsafe-eval'; script-src-attr 'unsafe-hashes' 'sha256-47DEQpj8HBSa+/TImW+5JCeuQeRkm5NMpJWZG3hSuFU='; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: https:; font-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self' https: wss:; worker-src blob: 'self'; object-src 'none'; frame-ancestors https://web.telegram.org https://*.telegram.org; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000

/tonconnect-manifest.json
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600
/logo.png
  Access-Control-Allow-Origin: *
